    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Formed on 22 May 1990 by the union of the conservative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> Arab Republic and the Marxist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</li><li>A brief democratic opening gave way to the 1994 civil war and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-abdullah-saleh">Saleh</a>'s long rule through tribal and military patronage.</li><li>Since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/houthi-movement">Houthis</a> seized Sanaa in 2014 it has been torn by war and one of the world's worst humanitarian crises.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1990 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> sat on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-security-council">UN Security Council</a> and voted against the resolution authorising force against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, a stand that cost hundreds of thousands of Yemenis their jobs in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

